quran[5]{c,v,t}:
  13,1,"Alif, Lam, Mim, Ra. These are the Verses of the Book. And what has been revealed to you from your Lord is the truth, but most people do not believe."
  13,2,"It is Allah Who raised the heavens without any pillars that you see. Then (befitting His Glory), He established His command on the Throne. And He subjected the sun and the moon, each orbiting for a specified time. He regulates the affairs (and) elaborates the signs (of creation) so that you may be certain of the meeting with your Lord."
  13,3,"He is the One Who has spread out the earth and placed firm mountains and rivers upon it. And of all the fruits, He has made therein a pair. He causes the night to cover the day. Indeed, there are signs for people who reflect."
  13,4,"And on the earth, there are (diverse) neighbouring tracks, vineyards, (various) farms and date palms growing from the same root and (others) from different roots. (All these are) irrigated by the same water. Yet We give some of them an advantage over others in taste and flavour. There are indeed signs in this for people who understand."
  13,5,"If you are to be amazed (at anything), then be amazed at their saying: ‘Once we have turned to dust, shall we be (raised) into a new creation?’ They are the ones who disbelieve in their Lord, and they shall have shackles around their necks. They shall be the inhabitants of the Fire. And they shall remain in it forever."
